# Dual-Bank OTA Bootloader — Implementation Plan

## Overview

Implement a custom dual-bank (A/B) OTA bootloader for the STM32F407VGTx so the Jetson Nano can remotely flash new firmware over the existing UART5 connection (9600 baud, 8N1). The bootloader occupies Sector 0 (16 KB), the application alternates between Bank A and Bank B, and boot configuration flags are stored in Sector 11.

---

## Flash Memory Layout (STM32F407VGTx — 1 MB)

```
Sector  Address Range             Size    Assignment
──────  ────────────────────────  ──────  ──────────────────────
  0     0x08000000 – 0x08003FFF   16 KB   BOOTLOADER
  1     0x08004000 – 0x08007FFF   16 KB   ┐
  2     0x08008000 – 0x0800BFFF   16 KB   │
  3     0x0800C000 – 0x0800FFFF   16 KB   │ BANK A (App Slot)
  4     0x08010000 – 0x0801FFFF   64 KB   │ Total: 496 KB
  5     0x08020000 – 0x0803FFFF  128 KB   │
  6     0x08040000 – 0x0805FFFF  128 KB   │
  7     0x08060000 – 0x0807FFFF  128 KB   ┘
  8     0x08080000 – 0x0809FFFF  128 KB   ┐
  9     0x080A0000 – 0x080BFFFF  128 KB   │ BANK B (App Slot)
 10     0x080C0000 – 0x080DFFFF  128 KB   ┘ Total: 384 KB
 11     0x080E0000 – 0x080FFFFF  128 KB   BOOT CONFIG FLAGS
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Bank B (384 KB) is smaller than Bank A (496 KB). The max app binary size is limited to **384 KB**. Your current OT_RTOS firmware is well under this limit.

---

## Boot Config Flags (Sector 11 — `0x080E0000`)

Stored as a 16-byte structure at the start of Sector 11:

```c
typedef struct {
    uint32_t magic;          // 0xB007F1A6 = valid config
    uint8_t  active_bank;    // 'A' (0x41) or 'B' (0x42)
    uint8_t  ota_requested;  // 0x01 = OTA pending, 0x00 = normal
    uint8_t  bank_a_valid;   // 0x01 = valid firmware in A
    uint8_t  bank_b_valid;   // 0x01 = valid firmware in B
    uint32_t bank_a_size;    // Firmware size in Bank A
    uint32_t bank_b_size;    // Firmware size in Bank B
} BootConfig_t;             // 16 bytes
```

On first flash (fresh MCU), Sector 11 is all `0xFF` → magic doesn't match → bootloader defaults to Bank A.

---

## OTA Protocol (Bootloader Mode — UART5, 9600 Baud)

Once the bootloader enters OTA mode, it uses a **dedicated binary protocol** (different from the app's `[0x2B...0x3B]` protocol) to avoid data byte conflicts.

### Packet Format (Nano → STM32)

```
[SOF_1(0xAA), SOF_2(0x55), CMD, PAYLOAD(N bytes), CRC8]
```

| CMD | Name | Payload | Purpose |
|-----|------|---------|---------|
| `0x01` | OTA_INFO | `fw_size(4B) + fw_crc32(4B)` = 8 bytes | Declare firmware size and expected CRC32 |
| `0x02` | OTA_DATA | `chunk_idx(2B) + data(128B)` = 130 bytes | Send firmware chunk (last chunk may be shorter) |
| `0x03` | OTA_END | 0 bytes | Signal transfer complete, trigger verification |

- CRC8: CRC-8/ATM (poly `0x07`, init `0x00`) computed over `[CMD, PAYLOAD]`
- Chunk size: 128 bytes (last chunk padded with `0xFF` to 128)

### Response Format (STM32 → Nano)

```
[SOF_1(0xAA), SOF_2(0x55), STATUS, DATA(2B)]
```

| STATUS | Name | DATA | Meaning |
|--------|------|------|---------|
| `0x01` | ACK_READY | `active_bank, target_bank` | Bootloader ready. Nano must use target_bank to pick `.bin` |
| `0x02` | ACK_OK | `chunk_idx(2B)` | Chunk received OK, send next |
| `0x03` | ACK_RESEND | `chunk_idx(2B)` | CRC failed, resend this chunk |
| `0x04` | ACK_SUCCESS | `0x00, 0x00` | OTA complete, firmware verified |
| `0x05` | ACK_FAIL | `error_code, 0x00` | OTA failed (error codes below) |

**Error codes:** `0x01`=CRC mismatch after 3 retries, `0x02`=size mismatch, `0x03`=flash write error, `0x04`=timeout

### Timing & Retry Logic

| Parameter | Value |
|-----------|-------|
| Receive timeout | **5 seconds** per packet (if no data, abort OTA) |
| CRC retry | **3 attempts** per chunk (send ACK_RESEND, wait for same chunk) |
| After 3 fails | Send ACK_FAIL (error `0x01`), abort OTA, jump to current active app |

---

## Complete OTA Flow (Active/Active)

```
       NANO SIDE                                  STM32 SIDE
           │                                          │
  Execute ota_updater.py <A.bin> <B.bin>              │ 
           │                                          │
  Send [0x2B, 0x71, 0x3B] ─────────────────────────► App running normally
           │                                          │
           │                                     App sets ota_requested=0x01
           │                                     App reboots (HAL_NVIC_SystemReset)
           │                                          │
  Wait 2 seconds                                 Bootloader starts
           │                                          │
           │ ◄─────────────────────────────────  Send ACK_READY [0x41(A), 0x42(B)]
           │                                          │
  Receive ACK_READY                                   │
  Observe target=Bank B                               │
  Select OT_RTOS_B.bin                                │
           │                                          │
  Send OTA_INFO (size, crc) ───────────────────────► Erase target bank
           │ ◄─────────────────────────────────────  Send ACK_OK
           │                                          │
  Send Chunk 0 ────────────────────────────────────► Verify / Write Flash
           │ ◄─────────────────────────────────────  Send ACK_OK
           │                 ...                      │
           │                 ...                      │
  Send Chunk N ────────────────────────────────────► Verify / Write Flash
           │ ◄─────────────────────────────────────  Send ACK_OK
           │                                          │
  Send OTA_END ────────────────────────────────────► Verify full firmware CRC32
           │ ◄─────────────────────────────────────  Send ACK_SUCCESS
           │                                          │
           │                                     Bootloader jumps to New Active Bank
```

---

## Proposed Changes

### Bootloader Project (New)

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The bootloader is a **separate STM32CubeIDE project**. Create it via CubeMX with only **UART5** enabled (9600, 8N1). No FreeRTOS, no ADC, no timers.

#### [NEW] [bootloader_main.c](file:///c:/Users/oml/Documents/BitBucket/MOT/MOT-CONTROLLER-CARD/OT_BOOTLOADER/Core/Src/bootloader_main.c)

Main bootloader logic (~150 lines):
- Read Boot Config → check `ota_requested` flag
- If OTA: init UART5, erase target bank, receive/write chunks, verify CRC32, update config, re-call self
- If normal: set `SCB->VTOR`, set `MSP`, jump to active bank's Reset_Handler

#### [NEW] [flash_ops.c](file:///c:/Users/oml/Documents/BitBucket/MOT/MOT-CONTROLLER-CARD/OT_BOOTLOADER/Core/Src/flash_ops.c) / [flash_ops.h](file:///c:/Users/oml/Documents/BitBucket/MOT/MOT-CONTROLLER-CARD/OT_BOOTLOADER/Core/Inc/flash_ops.h)

Flash operations (~100 lines):
- [flash_erase_bank(bank)](file:///c:/Users/oml/Documents/BitBucket/MOT/MOT-STM32-BOOTLOADER/OT_Bootloader/Core/Src/flash_ops.c#80-118) — erase sectors 1-7 (Bank A) or 8-10 (Bank B)
- [flash_write(address, data, length)](file:///c:/Users/oml/Documents/BitBucket/MOT/MOT-STM32-BOOTLOADER/OT_Bootloader/Core/Src/flash_ops.c#123-164) — word-aligned write
- [flash_read_config()](file:///c:/Users/oml/Documents/BitBucket/MOT/MOT-STM32-BOOTLOADER/OT_Bootloader/Core/Src/flash_ops.c#15-37) / [flash_write_config()](file:///c:/Users/oml/Documents/BitBucket/MOT/MOT-STM32-BOOTLOADER/OT_Bootloader/Core/Src/flash_ops.c#38-75) — read/write Boot Config in Sector 11
- [flash_crc32(address, length)](file:///c:/Users/oml/Documents/BitBucket/MOT/MOT-STM32-BOOTLOADER/OT_Bootloader/Core/Src/flash_ops.c#169-188) — compute CRC32 over flash region

#### [NEW] [ota_protocol.c](file:///c:/Users/oml/Documents/BitBucket/MOT/MOT-CONTROLLER-CARD/OT_BOOTLOADER/Core/Src/ota_protocol.c) / [ota_protocol.h](file:///c:/Users/oml/Documents/BitBucket/MOT/MOT-CONTROLLER-CARD/OT_BOOTLOADER/Core/Inc/ota_protocol.h)

OTA UART communication (~120 lines):
- `ota_wait_packet(timeout_ms)` — receive a packet with SOF detection + CRC8 validation
- `ota_send_ack(status, data)` — send 5-byte response
- [ota_receive_firmware()](file:///c:/Users/oml/Documents/BitBucket/MOT/MOT-STM32-BOOTLOADER/OT_Bootloader/Core/Src/ota_protocol.c#151-317) — main OTA loop: OTA_INFO → chunks with retry → OTA_END → verify
- [crc8_atm()](file:///c:/Users/oml/Documents/BitBucket/MOT/MOT-CONTROLLER-CARD/OT_RTOS/Core/Src/main.c#379-396) / [crc32()](file:///c:/Users/oml/Documents/BitBucket/MOT/MOT-STM32-BOOTLOADER/OT_Bootloader/Core/Src/flash_ops.c#169-188) — checksum functions

#### [NEW] [STM32F407VGTX_FLASH.ld](file:///c:/Users/oml/Documents/BitBucket/MOT/MOT-CONTROLLER-CARD/OT_BOOTLOADER/STM32F407VGTX_FLASH.ld)

Bootloader linker script — restrict flash to Sector 0 only:
```
FLASH (rx) : ORIGIN = 0x08000000, LENGTH = 16K
```

