### Nano-Side OTA Script (New)

#### [NEW] [ota_updater.py](file:///c:/Users/oml/Documents/BitBucket/MOT/MOT-PROCESSOR-CARD/modules/ota_updater.py)

Python script (~150 lines) to send firmware from Nano to STM32:
1. Send OTA_START command `[0x2B, 0x71, 0x3B]` to app (existing protocol)
2. Wait 2s for STM32 reboot
3. Wait for ACK_READY from bootloader
4. Send OTA_INFO (firmware size + CRC32)
5. Send firmware in 128-byte chunks with per-chunk CRC8
6. Handle ACK_RESEND (retry up to 3 times per chunk)
7. Send OTA_END
8. Wait for ACK_SUCCESS or ACK_FAIL
9. Log progress percentage to console

---

## First-Time Flash Procedure

1. Build bootloader project → `OT_BOOTLOADER.elf` (fits in 16 KB)
2. Build app project → `OT_RTOS.bin` (starts at `0x08004000`)
3. Flash via ST-Link:
   ```bash
   # Flash bootloader to 0x08000000
   openocd -f interface/stlink.cfg -f target/stm32f4x.cfg \
     -c "program OT_BOOTLOADER.elf verify reset exit"

   # Flash app to Bank A at 0x08004000
   openocd -f interface/stlink.cfg -f target/stm32f4x.cfg \
     -c "program OT_RTOS.bin 0x08004000 verify reset exit"
   ```
4. Boot Config (Sector 11) is all `0xFF` → bootloader defaults: `active_bank=A`, `ota_requested=0`

---

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
1. Build bootloader project — verify it fits within 16 KB
2. Build OT_RTOS with modified linker — verify binary starts at `0x08004000`
3. Run CRC8/CRC32 unit tests on PC (compare known vectors)

### Hardware Testing
1. Flash bootloader + app via ST-Link → verify app boots normally (lights, sensors work)
2. Send OTA_START from Nano → verify STM32 reboots into bootloader, sends ACK_READY
3. Send a small test firmware (~1 KB) → verify chunk ACKs and final CRC32 pass
4. Verify new firmware boots after OTA
5. Test failure cases: corrupt a chunk CRC → verify 3 retries then ACK_FAIL
6. Test timeout: stop sending mid-transfer → verify bootloader aborts after 5s, boots old app
7. Test power-cycle during OTA → verify old app still boots
